Article 4 Social expert evaluation, testing, and assessment institutions that voluntarily accept entrustment by a People's Court to engage in judicial expert evaluation and apply to enter the roster of judicial expert evaluators of the People's Court shall submit an application and the following materials to the judicial expert evaluation institution of the People's Court:
(1) copy of the business license of the enterprise or social organization legal person;
(2) professional qualification certificate;
(3) list of professional and technical personnel, their practice qualifications, and main achievements;
(4) annual inspection documents;
(5) other necessary documents and materials.

Article 5 Professional and technical personnel who, in their personal capacity, voluntarily accept entrustment by a People's Court to engage in judicial expert evaluation and apply to enter the roster of judicial expert evaluators of the People's Court shall submit an application and the following materials to the judicial expert evaluation institution of the People's Court:
(1) letter of introduction from the employing unit;
(2) professional qualification certificate;
(3) proof of main achievements;
(4) other necessary documents and materials, etc.

Article 9 The expert evaluators who have been included in the roster shall undergo the annual review by the judicial expert evaluation institution of the relevant People's Court, and shall submit the following materials:
(1) annual business work report;
(2) changes in professional and technical personnel;
(3) updates of instruments and equipment;
(4) other changes and materials required to be submitted.
If there are changes in the annual review, the relevant judicial expert evaluation institution shall report them level by level to the judicial expert evaluation institution of the Supreme People's Court for record.
